* CHARMM c52 testcase block_cats.inp
* BLOCK's CATS subcommand must reach BLOCK, and the top-level string
* concatenation command must keep working.
*

! (A line holding nothing but a star ends the title block, so the rest of
! this description is written as ordinary comments.)
!
! BLOCK> CATS selects the constrained atoms that lambda-dynamics is allowed
! to scale (lambdadyn.F90, ldm_call_catsmsld_setup).  A top-level command
! named CATS was added in c52 to concatenate strings (machio.F90, STRCAT).
! BLOCK reads its subcommands by calling MISCOM first, so any word MISCOM
! claims is taken away from BLOCK before BLOCK ever sees it, and for the
! time both were called CATS a CATS line inside BLOCK ... END was silently
! handled by STRCAT.  The concatenation command is now called STRC.
!
! Three things went wrong, none of them announced:
!
!   1. The constrained-atom selection never happened.  nires stayed 0 and
!      iblcks was never filled, so lambda-dynamics scaled nothing.  A whole
!      residue mutation set up this way ran with the wrong forces and
!      finished without complaint.  That is the reason this matters.
!
!   2. STRCAT takes the first word after the keyword as a parameter name
!      and concatenates the rest into it, so `CATS sele type C* end'
!      defined a parameter called SELE, overwriting whatever was there.
!
!   3. Neither raised a warning, because STRCAT's syntax is satisfied by a
!      name followed by at least one word.

if ?block .ne. 1 then
   echo BLOCK_CATS TESTCASE RESULT: SKIP
   stop
endif

stream datadir.def

! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! A small system: three residues of three atoms each.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! Three because MSLD needs at least three blocks -- one for the
! environment and two alchemical states at a site -- and checks 6 and 7 need
! MSLD switched on for the CATS energy term to be evaluated at all.
!
! The two selections used below have to give different counts, or check 5
! could not tell a working CATS from an intercepted one: the last CALL
! picks the 3 atoms of residue 3, CATS picks the 2 hydrogens of residue 2,
! and ?NSEL is left holding whichever of them ran last.

read rtf card
* minimal
*
   99  1
mass 1  HT  1.00800 H
mass 2  CT 12.01100 C

resi ALA2  0.00
group
atom C1 CT  0.00
atom H1 HT  0.00
atom H2 HT  0.00
bond C1 H1  C1 H2
patch first none last none

end

read param card flex
* minimal
*
atoms
mass 1  HT  1.00800 H
mass 2  CT 12.01100 C

bonds
CT HT  300.0 1.09

angles
HT CT HT  35.0 109.5

nonbonded
HT  0.0 -0.0220 1.32
CT  0.0 -0.0200 2.28

end

read sequence ALA2 3
generate MAIN setup warn first none last none

read coor card
* three molecules, far enough apart to be uninteresting
*
    9
    1    1 ALA2 C1     0.00000   0.00000   0.00000 MAIN 1      0.00000
    2    1 ALA2 H1     1.09000   0.00000   0.00000 MAIN 1      0.00000
    3    1 ALA2 H2    -0.36000   1.02800   0.00000 MAIN 1      0.00000
    4    2 ALA2 C1    10.00000   0.00000   0.00000 MAIN 2      0.00000
    5    2 ALA2 H1    11.09000   0.00000   0.00000 MAIN 2      0.00000
    6    2 ALA2 H2     9.64000   1.02800   0.00000 MAIN 2      0.00000
    7    3 ALA2 C1    20.00000   0.00000   0.00000 MAIN 3      0.00000
    8    3 ALA2 H1    21.09000   0.00000   0.00000 MAIN 3      0.00000
    9    3 ALA2 H2    19.64000   1.02800   0.00000 MAIN 3      0.00000

! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! Check 1: the top-level command still concatenates
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! This is what it was added for -- building a case-sensitive path out of
! pieces -- and 34 SCC-DFTB testcases depend on it.  If a fix for the
! collision goes too far and removes the command, this check says so.
!
! Both sides are built the same way, because an unquoted word in an `if'
! is upper-cased by the parser while a parameter keeps the case it was
! given; comparing against a bare literal would test the parser, not STRC.

strc joined "abc" "def"
strc expect "abcdef"
set ok = 0
if @joined eq @expect then set ok = 1
@testcheck @ok 1 -0.5 BLOCK_CATS_STRC_CONCATENATES

! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! Checks 2 and 3: quoting preserves case, and the quotes do not survive
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! These are the two halves of what the SCC-DFTB parameter paths rely on,
! and they are checked separately so a failure says which one broke.
!
! Case: the quoted and unquoted forms of the same text must NOT agree.
! The parser upper-cases the unquoted one, and stripping the quotes is
! what keeps the other as written.  If both came through upper-cased,
! every parameter path built with this command would silently become
! upper case and fail to open.  (`set' upper-cases too, so there is no
! way to write a case-preserved literal to compare against -- the
! unquoted form is the only available reference.)
!
! Quotes: the same text given as one quoted word and as two must agree.
! If the quotes were left in the value, the one-word form would be
! "aBcD" and the two-word form "aB""cD", which differ.

strc quoted "aBcD"
strc bare aBcD
set ok = 0
if @quoted ne @bare then set ok = 1
@testcheck @ok 1 -0.5 BLOCK_CATS_STRC_PRESERVES_CASE

strc split "aB" "cD"
set ok = 0
if @quoted eq @split then set ok = 1
@testcheck @ok 1 -0.5 BLOCK_CATS_STRC_STRIPS_QUOTES

! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! Checks 4 and 5: CATS inside a BLOCK belongs to BLOCK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! SELEGUARD is a sentinel in the parameter that STRCAT would overwrite.
! If the CATS line reaches BLOCK the sentinel survives, because BLOCK's
! CATS reads an atom selection and defines no parameters.  If MISCOM
! claims the line first, STRCAT writes the concatenated remainder into
! SELE and the sentinel is gone.
!
! ?NSEL is the other half of the same story and the one that matters:
! BLOCK's CATS calls SELCTA, which publishes the number of atoms it
! selected.  An intercepted CATS never calls it, so ?NSEL still holds the
! 3 atoms of the last CALL rather than the 2 hydrogens CATS asked for.

! One BLOCK setup serves checks 4, 5, 6 and 7.  CATS is the last thing in it
! that makes a selection, so ?NSEL afterwards is the one CATS made.
! `ldin' switches lambda dynamics on, and `SCAT K' gives the restraint a
! force constant, which checks 6 and 7 need.

set sele SELEGUARD

! The order of the subcommands below is the order every working MSLD test
! uses (c45test/domdec_minimize.inp, c51test/blade_msld_piecewise.inp) and
! it matters: `lang' has to precede `ldin', which is what makes `ldin' read
! the fifth number, and `ldbi' has to be given or the biasing-potential
! count is never initialized.  SCAT and CATS come last so that the
! selection CATS makes is the one ?NSEL reports.

BLOCK 3
   CALL 2 SELE resid 2 END
   CALL 3 SELE resid 3 END
   qldm theta
   lang temp 298.0
   ldin 1 1.0 0.0 5.0 0.0 5.0
   ldin 2 0.5 0.0 5.0 0.0 5.0
   ldin 3 0.5 0.0 5.0 0.0 5.0
   excl 2 3
   rmla bond thet dihe impr
   msld 0 1 1
   msma
   ldbi 0
   SCAT ON
   SCAT K 10.0
   CATS sele resid 2 .and. type H* end
END

set seleafter @sele
set nselafter ?NSEL

set ok = 0
if @seleafter eq SELEGUARD then set ok = 1
@testcheck @ok 1 -0.5 BLOCK_CATS_NOT_INTERCEPTED

@testcheck @nselafter 2 -0.5 BLOCK_CATS_SELECTED_ITS_OWN_ATOMS

! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! Checks 6 and 7: the selection reaches the energy
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! The checks above show CATS was parsed by BLOCK.  This one shows the
! result is actually used.  msld_add_restraints (lambdadyn.F90) harmonically
! restrains every atom CATS selected to the centre of mass of its group, and
! reports the total in the CATS energy term.  It loops over nires groups, so
! an intercepted CATS leaves nires at 0, the loop body never runs, and the
! CATS energy is identically zero however the system moves.
!
! No reference value is needed or wanted: the restraint is 0.5*k*|r-com|^2
! summed over the selected atoms, which is positive for any selection whose
! atoms are not all at one point, and exactly zero when the selection never
! happened.  Asserting "greater than zero" is the whole of the physics and
! holds whatever the geometry and the force constant are.

energy
set ecats0 = ?CATS

! A short run, so the term is exercised through the integrator as well as
! through a single energy call.  Lambda dynamics insists on a unit to write
! the lambda trajectory to, so it gets one in the scratch directory.
open unit 24 write file name @9block_cats.lmd

dynamics leap start nstep 20 timestep 0.001 -
   nprint 10 iprfrq 20 -
   firstt 100.0 finalt 100.0 iasvel 1 iseed 314159 -
   inbfrq 5 ihbfrq 0 -
   iunldm 24 nsavl 10 -
   iunread -1 iunwrite -1 iuncrd -1 iunvel -1 nsavc 0 nsavv 0

energy
set ecats1 = ?CATS

set ok = 0
if @ecats0 gt 0.0 then set ok = 1
@testcheck @ok 1 -0.5 BLOCK_CATS_ENERGY_IS_NONZERO

set ok = 0
if @ecats1 gt 0.0 then set ok = 1
@testcheck @ok 1 -0.5 BLOCK_CATS_ENERGY_SURVIVES_DYNAMICS

stop
